+- Report the findings **verbatim**, by rule name. The eleven rules in
+  `GATE_RULES` (`lib/gate.mjs`) mean different things and the operator acts on
+  which one fired:
+  - `check_failed` — a declared check command exited non-zero (or the worker
+    was killed at the wall cap; see below).
+  - `ac_unmapped` — an acceptance criterion has no `ac_map` entry and no
+    unverifiable marker.
+  - `ac_failed` — an `ac_map` entry's command exited non-zero.
+  - `ac_unsatisfiable` — the worker declared the criterion itself cannot be
+    satisfied, with evidence.
+  - `unverifiable_no_reason` — a criterion was marked unverifiable with no
+    reason given.
+  - `mapping_implausible` — an `ac_map` entry's command doesn't plausibly test
+    the criterion it claims to.
+  - `unbacked_claim` — a claim of success with no command backing it.
+  - `scope_violation` — the diff touches a path outside what the ticket
+    permitted.
+  - `off_limits` — the diff touches a path the config declared off limits.
+  - `evidence_weakened` — a check went green by removing what it looks at.
+  - `instrument_modified` — a check went green by editing the checker itself.
